;
; BIND zone file for chattr.at.
; → Cloudflare: Add a site → chattr.at → "Import DNS records" → upload this file.
;   (Cloudflare ignores the SOA/NS below and provides its own nameservers; it
;    imports the A/CNAME records.) Then switch the Netcup nameservers to the two
;    Cloudflare NS that CF shows you.
;
; The landing (Craft CMS) runs on nc-chattr = <prod-host>.
; The app/api currently stay on chattr.geraldhofbauer.net — the commented
; records at the bottom are for the LATER chattr.at cutover of the clients.

$ORIGIN chattr.at.
$TTL 3600

@   IN  SOA ns.chattr.at. hostmaster.chattr.at. (
            2026072801 ; serial (YYYYMMDDnn)
            7200       ; refresh
            3600       ; retry
            1209600    ; expire
            3600 )     ; minimum

; Nameservers — PLACEHOLDERS. Cloudflare assigns the real pair when you add the
; zone; set those two at Netcup. (Left here only to keep the file a valid zone.)
@   IN  NS  ns1.example-cloudflare.com.
@   IN  NS  ns2.example-cloudflare.com.

; ── Landing: chattr.at + www → Craft CMS on nc-chattr ──────────────────────
@       IN  A       <prod-host>
www     IN  CNAME   chattr.at.

; ── (optional, later) client cutover from chattr.geraldhofbauer.net ────────
; Uncomment when you move the app/api over to the chattr.at domain:
;api    IN  A       <prod-host>
;app    IN  A       <prod-host>
